1. Logging In (az login)
To authenticate your Azure CLI session:

Bash
az login
Useful Options:
Tenant Specific Login: If your account belongs to multiple Entra ID (Azure AD) tenants:

Bash
az login --tenant <tenant-id-or-domain>
Service Principal Login (for CI/CD pipelines):

Bash
az login --service-principal -u <app-id> -p <secret-or-certificate> --tenant <tenant-id>
Device Code Login (for headless environments/remote SSH):

Bash
az login --use-device-code
2. Managing Subscriptions (az account)
Since your Bicep framework deploys at the Subscription scope, target the correct subscription before executing az deployment sub create.

List Available Subscriptions
To view all subscriptions your account has access to:

Bash
az account list --output table
To see all subscriptions including disabled/inactive ones:

Bash
az account list --all --output table
View Current Active Subscription
To confirm which subscription your commands will currently target:

Bash
az account show --output table
Set/Switch Active Subscription
To switch your active CLI context to the target subscription where you want to deploy the policies:

By Subscription ID:

Bash
az account set --subscription "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
By Subscription Name:

Bash
az account set --subscription "My-Target-Subscription-Name"
Complete Deployment Sequence
Combining authentication, subscription targeting, and deployment:

Bash
# 1. Authenticate to Azure
az login

# 2. Target the correct subscription
az account set --subscription "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"

# 3. Verify target context
az account show --output table

# 4. Deploy your Policy-as-Code framework
az deployment sub create \
  --location westeurope \
  --template-file main.bicep \
  --parameters '@deploymentParameters.json'
